          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 19: [dec] × 6 (6 st). FO leaving 15 cm tail for closure. (6 sts)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Antennae (make 2)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chain 8 in sage green, then work 1 dc in each of the last 7 chains back to the base. Fasten off."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Assembly"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Insert "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "safety-eyes"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "safety eyes"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " at the front tip of the body, 1.5 cm apart. Stuff the body so the wide base sits flat. Stuff the shell firmly. Set the shell on the upper back of the body with about one third of its base resting on the body. Sew the shell down with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "amigurumi-decrease"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "ladder stitch"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", catching both layers all the way round. Attach the antennae 1 cm apart at the crown."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "surface-embroidery"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "surface embroidery"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " in cream from the shell centre outward in loose chain stitches. Two or three rotations make a clear spiral. Weave in all ends. Add two straight stitches in black at each antenna tip for eyes if stalk eyes are not available."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Try the mushroom next as a scene prop, or the hedgehog for another small creature."
          }
        ]
      }
